<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summon Animal</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Ranger (guild level 40, up to 70%)
Mana: 40
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast summon animal &lt;animal&gt;
tell &lt;animal&gt; &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>The caster utters 'Ad voce vene', and an animal from anywhere in the 
world appears in answer to the call, wakes and follows its summoner. It 
serves just as a charmed animal does (see <a cmd='#'>Help Charm Animal</a>): command it 
with tell, for example tell bear kill orc. It won't attack another player 
unless both of you have signed the Book of Blood, and after a while it 
returns to the wild; a strong dispel magic ends the service at once.
</p><p>Only animals answer: beasts, birds, reptiles, amphibians, insects and 
worms. The animal resists with its brain against yours and your skill in 
the spell. You must be alone (immortals aside), out in the open, and you 
can have only one animal in your service at a time. Some places, at 
either end, prevent the summoning. You must be standing. It is also found 
on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
